  "ref": "ACT.23.11",
  "review_notes": [
    "Corrected the placement of by in stood by him: the accepted alignment read it as the preverb ἐπι-, but rule 106 scopes that arm to a particle no other source token answers to, and ἐφίστημι here governs the bare dative αὐτῷ. ACT.4.1 ἐπέστησαν αὐτοῖς → came / upon them is the rule's own precedent for this very lemma, and ACT.23.33 παρέστησαν … αὐτῷ → before him already reads the chapter's parallel that way. Nothing else in the verse changes."
